<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“There you guys are!”</span> She laughs, patting <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> on the head and walking over to her husband, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I got the pizzas like you asked, must be a big day if we’re getting this many. Where have you guys been?”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">Despite his back being to you, you can see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> freeze in place at his mom’s question.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The award ceremony… remember?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad replies gently. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> won that Hero Award. Did you see it on TV like you said you would?”</span> His mom looks at him confused for a moment, <span style="Color: Yellow">her eyes moving back and forth between his eyes as if the information is running through several filters.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, right!”</span> She slaps her forehead and laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, just so tired. The doctor was going on and on-”</span> She walks over to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, patting him on the head. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m so proud of you! Sorry I couldn’t make it. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> was jumping on the trampoline and I tried to tell him it was time to go, but you know how he is. Then he fell off and twisted his ankle! Poor thing, had to run him to the doctor. Thankfully, he said it should be fine. He’s resting it right now, but I’m sure he’ll love to see your trophy! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>! Your brother’s back, come out here!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We should let him rest.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad quickly steps over, putting his hands on his wife’s shoulders, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He doesn’t even like pizza, right?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No, no… It’s chicken he doesn’t like. I don’t blame him, that paste was…”</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">She pauses for a moment, glancing towards the hallway.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We really gotta talk to that boy about ignoring us. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>!”</span> She sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, could you go get your brother please? He may be having trouble walking on his ankle.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“How about you go in there with your precious little baby and we’ll stay out here and celebrate the one that matters?”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s reply is harsh and direct, causing his father to quickly snap towards him,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You know, your other son? <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>? The one who won an award? The one who actually does stuff? Ring a bell? We saved you a seat, you know? Since you said you’d be there!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, that’s enough.”</span> His father responds, <span style="Color: Yellow">though his wife stands back up looking towards the hallway and sighs.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“There will be other awards, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>.”</span> His mother responds with a wave of her hand, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You boys have your father and me outnumbered, we aren’t going to be able to make every single little event.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“How about making one?”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> takes a step forward, the tension becoming so thick you can practically see it.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>! I said that’s enough!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s father responds even harsher this time, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“She’s trying.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Not hard enough! This is bullshit, why do we-!?”</span> <br>

