<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey mom!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly dashes over with a smile, <span style="Color: LightCoral">putting himself between all three of them,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Did you see my award? It’s pretty cool, right? It has my name and everything.”</span> His mom looks down at him in surprise before smiling. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, would you look at that!”</span> She laughs, leaning down to inspect the award, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s so nice! We should put it on the shelf next to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s soccer trophy!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Y- yeah…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> pauses, <span style="Color: LightCoral">shoulders slumping slightly.</span> He then suddenly smiles again, reaching into his pocket and pulling out a folded piece of paper. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, yeah! They took a picture of me getting the award, look! I’m wearing those nice clothes you bought me. I asked <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> if he could print out a copy, since you still have that old picture in your wallet and- well, I thought it would be nice for you to have a new one! Isn’t it nice?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles widely as his mother takes the photo, cooing at it. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh my, those clothes fit perfectly! My little handsome man!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s smile grows as she dotes over the picture, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I can’t believe how big you’ve gotten! My little baby, all grown up and dressed so sharply! Oh, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>, this is beautiful, thank you!”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">There is a pause in the room, a chill falling over it as if all the life and warmth was suddenly sucked out. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You know, I always knew you’d make a handsome young man. And now you’re getting and award for…”</span> She pauses, staring down at the picture, a mixture of confusion and pain in her face as she tries to process what she’s looking at.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Charity? No… no, he’s not…” <br>
<br>
She stares blankly at the picture for a long moment…</span> <br>
<br>

