    <span style="Color: LightCoral">CRASH! <br>
    <br>
    The sudden noise snaps you all back to your senses. You see a blur run past you, towards the back door. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>!”</span> His dad calls out, taking a step to the glass sliding door before stopping, sighing in defeat. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“She couldn’t even give him one night.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> spits, looking at his mother, a mixture of anger and sadness in his eyes.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s all he wanted, but you had to coddle her. This is bullshit, it would be better if she wasn’t even here!”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, I-!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad steps towards his eldest son, <span style="Color: LightCoral">but the boy quickly stomps down the hall to his room, slamming the door shut. The man then falls onto the counter stool, burying his head in his hands as you stand there awkwardly. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s mom snaps out of whatever stupor she was in, dropping the photo and looking at the pizza boxes. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh! Right, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> asked me to bring him a few slices of ham to his room. His ankle is still bugging him, so we don’t want him on it. You guys help yourselves; I’m going to make sure he’s doing alright and I’ll be back.”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">She walks off with a plain slice of pizza on a plate, smiling and humming to herself as she walks towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s room, opening the door and turning the light on as she steps inside. <br>

